  "description": "From the University of Alaska Fairbanks on trails and dirt and paved roads: west over the Skarland trails and past Ballaine Lake, up the long climb to Ester Dome (the Ascent), an out-and-back along the ridge to the turnaround, the steep chute and long birch-forest descent, Henderson and Goldhill Roads, and back across campus to the finish. Downhills are flat on a treadmill without decline. Unofficial.",
