    "notes": "The course as run since 2021. Route traced over OpenStreetMap trails and roads following the community-maintained Equinox Marathon Trail relation in its stored course order; the course is uncertified, so distances are scaled to 26.2 miles between the ridge turnaround (15.1 miles) and the finish. Elevations from the 2017 Fairbanks bare-earth lidar, which follows the trail bed under the forest; the official \"about 3,300 ft\" of gain comes from a coarser 2002 profile. Downhills, including the long descent from Ester Dome, are flat on a treadmill without decline. Unofficial.",
